      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason that `shortName` was added is because the OEM will pass a system property for ddr size with the format: 100GB, 900MB, 90000KB and we need to parse that string and based on the units, convert it to bytes. We could have something like\n\n```java\n    public static long getDdrSizeInBytes(@NonNull String ddrSize) {\n        Pattern pattern \u003d\n                Pattern.compile(\"^(([1-9]{1}[0-9]{0,3})(KB|MB|GB))$\");\n        Matcher matcher \u003d pattern.matcher(ddrSize);\n        if (matcher.matches()) {\n            long size \u003d Long.parseLong(matcher.group(2));\n            String unit \u003d matcher.group(3);\n            if (\"KB\".equals(unit) { \n               return KILOBYTE.toBytes(size);\n            } else if(\"MB\".equals(unit) { \n               return MEGABYTE.toBytes(size);\n            } else {\n               return GIGABYTE.toBytes(size);\n            }\n            return du.toBytes(size);\n        }\n\n        return 0;\n```\n\nHowever, if we add the property \"shortName\" to the enum, we could have:\n\n```java\n    public static long getDdrSizeInBytes(@NonNull String ddrSize) {\n        Pattern pattern \u003d\n                Pattern.compile(\"^(([1-9]{1}[0-9]{0,3})(KB|MB|GB))$\");\n        Matcher matcher \u003d pattern.matcher(ddrSize);\n        if (matcher.matches()) {\n            long size \u003d Long.parseLong(matcher.group(2));\n            DataUnit du \u003d DataUnit.fromShortName(matcher.group(3));\n\n            return du.toBytes(size);\n        }\n\n        return 0;\n```\n\nThe `shortName` property follows a similar pattern found in the ChronoUnit class:\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:libcore/ojluni/src/main/java/java/time/temporal/ChronoUnit.java;l\u003d83",
